=== accelerator-jira --help ===
Usage: accelerator-jira <COMMAND>

Commands:
  create          Create an issue
  update          Update an issue's summary and body
  show            Show an issue as JSON, rendering ADF fields to Markdown
  search          Search issues, rendering Jira's verbatim envelope
  comment         Comment on an issue
  transition      Transition an issue to a named workflow state
  attach          Attach files to an issue
  init            Verify credentials, discover the catalogue, or list its parts
  fields          Refresh, resolve or list the custom-field cache
  resolve-fields  Resolve the issue type and project for a create, as a tab-separated line
  help            Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

=== accelerator-jira create --help ===
Create an issue

Usage: accelerator-jira create [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --summary <SUMMARY>
          

      --type <TYPE>
          

      --project <PROJECT>
          

      --body-file <BODY_FILE>
          

      --assignee <ASSIGNEE>
          

      --emit <EMIT>
          The stdout projection: the full JSON, or the bare key for a writeback

          Possible values:
          - json: The full issue JSON envelope (the default)
          - key:  Only the bare validated key, for a frontmatter writeback
          
          [default: json]

  -q, --quiet
          

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

=== accelerator-jira update --help ===
Update an issue's summary and body

Usage: accelerator-jira update [OPTIONS] <KEY>

Arguments:
  <KEY>  

Options:
      --summary <SUMMARY>      
      --body-file <BODY_FILE>  
  -q, --quiet                  
  -h, --help                   Print help

=== accelerator-jira show --help ===
Show an issue as JSON, rendering ADF fields to Markdown

Usage: accelerator-jira show [OPTIONS] <KEY>

Arguments:
  <KEY>  

Options:
      --comments <COMMENTS>  Include the most recent N comments (0-100)
      --fields <FIELDS>      The field selection query (default `*all`) [default: *all]
      --expand <EXPAND>      The expand query (default `names,schema,transitions`) [default: names,schema,transitions]
      --render-adf           Render ADF fields to Markdown (on by default)
      --no-render-adf        
  -h, --help                 Print help

=== accelerator-jira search --help ===
Search issues, rendering Jira's verbatim envelope

Usage: accelerator-jira search [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --project <PROJECT>        
      --all-projects             
      --status <STATUSES>        
      --label <LABELS>           
      --assignee <ASSIGNEES>     
      --type <TYPES>             
      --component <COMPONENTS>   
      --reporter <REPORTERS>     
      --parent <PARENTS>         
      --text <TEXTS>             
      --watching                 
      --jql <JQL>                
      --field <FIELDS>           
      --limit <LIMIT>            [default: 50]
      --page-token <PAGE_TOKEN>  
      --render-adf               Render ADF fields in the results to Markdown (off by default)
  -q, --quiet                    
  -h, --help                     Print help

=== accelerator-jira comment --help ===
Comment on an issue

Usage: accelerator-jira comment <COMMAND>

Commands:
  add     Add a comment to an issue
  list    List an issue's comments as a paginated envelope
  edit    Edit an existing comment
  delete  Delete a comment
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

=== accelerator-jira transition --help ===
Transition an issue to a named workflow state

Usage: accelerator-jira transition [OPTIONS] <KEY> [STATE]

Arguments:
  <KEY>    
  [STATE]  The target state name, positional or via `--state`

Options:
      --state <STATE>                  
      --transition-id <TRANSITION_ID>  
      --resolution <RESOLUTION>        
      --comment <COMMENT>              
      --no-notify                      
  -q, --quiet                          
  -h, --help                           Print help

=== accelerator-jira attach --help ===
Attach files to an issue

Usage: accelerator-jira attach [OPTIONS] <KEY> <FILES>...

Arguments:
  <KEY>       
  <FILES>...  

Options:
  -q, --quiet  
  -h, --help   Print help

=== accelerator-jira init --help ===
Verify credentials, discover the catalogue, or list its parts

Usage: accelerator-jira init <COMMAND>

Commands:
  verify          Verify credentials and cache the site identity, without printing them
  discover        Discover the project and field catalogue, caching it
  prompt-default  Print the resolved default project
  refresh-fields  Refresh the custom-field cache
  list-projects   List the cached projects
  list-fields     List the cached fields
  help            Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

=== accelerator-jira fields --help ===
Refresh, resolve or list the custom-field cache

Usage: accelerator-jira fields <COMMAND>

Commands:
  refresh  Refresh the custom-field cache from the live tracker
  resolve  Resolve one field name or id to its field id
  list     List the cached fields
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

=== accelerator-jira resolve-fields --help ===
Resolve the issue type and project for a create, as a tab-separated line

Usage: accelerator-jira resolve-fields [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --file <FILE>        A work-item file whose frontmatter seeds the resolution
      --kind <KIND>        An explicit kind (story|bug|epic|task|spike)
      --project <PROJECT>  An explicit project key
      --id <ID>            A project-coded id the project can be read from
  -h, --help               Print help

